{"kind":"request","text":"Is Goose's MCP Apps support sufficient for dap's purposes?\n\nScope: Hugh asks, 1 November 20:29 EST, to validate this. You have UI control and may use the `goose` application (https://goose-docs.ai/), including reconfiguring its MCP servers as needed.\n\nWhy it matters: three faults in the card reached only a person in the desktop AI app, each costing a person's session. If a second real host can run the cards under your control, you find such faults yourself, and dap's views are shown to work on more than one host. The answer can also be no, or sufficient for only part of this.\n\nRun the real `apps/views/src/node.ts` in Goose against dap-demo, and answer each row with what you observed. Label each row as observed in Goose, read from Goose's source or docs, or not reached:\n1. Does it negotiate the MCP Apps extension, and does it render a `ui://` card from a resource with no `_meta.ui.domain`?\n2. App-only tools: are `view_read` and `view_act` hidden from the model, and can the card call them?\n3. How many server processes does it start, and which one does a card's call reach?\n4. Does the card get its tool input and result? Does the host keep or drop `structuredContent`? Does the fallback text work?\n5. A press that takes 40 s, and a press past the card's 120 s wait: does the host cut the call?\n6. An answer's size limit, at the largest real answer you can make.\n7. `ui/update-model-context`, `ui/message`, display modes, resize, theme and CSP.\n8. A native act: Request changes or Approve through a card, with its receipt.\n9. A reload or a reopened chat: what happens to a card and its view.\n10. All four views: needs you, work, decision and change, with diff and interdiff.\n\nThe result, in a note: for each of dap's purposes, say sufficient, sufficient with a named gap, or not sufficient. Those purposes are: a builder's own test host in place of a person's session, a second supported host for people, and an agent host. Say which earlier person-session checks Goose could have caught, including the sandbox domain, the two processes and the 10-second press. Say what stays with the desktop AI app, since Goose is not that app. Where a difference comes from a Goose defect, name it, and do not change dap to fit one host without asking me.\n\nLimits:\n- Use a new scratch room and scratch homes. Never use the real room's owner home in Goose, and do not sign in the real room. Reads of dap-demo are fine, and acts go only to your scratch room.\n- A model provider for Goose may need a key or cost money. Use what is already configured. If it needs a credential you do not hold, tell me and stop that row.\n- Keep your Goose configuration changes listed, and put the configuration back when you finish. Hold no token, link or private text in evidence.\n- This builds no dap source. If a fault is in dap, file it as your own item, and do not fix it in this head.\n\nDone when the note and its sealed evidence pass the checker's review and land. It needs no deployment.\n\nOrder: next, after the row press lands and its scene is rerun. Ahead of the actor chip, because its answer may change how the remaining card work gets tested.","body":{"conditions":"A note says for each of dap's purposes whether Goose's MCP Apps support is sufficient, from observed rows with sealed evidence, approved by the checker and landed on main, with Goose's configuration restored.","target_head":"489adb02e256900abae1a6d02ef71ea4210959d5","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}